For this homework assignment, i first had to figure out how to get my spotlight to work. it was fairly simple, as all i had to do was update the proper uniforms in order for the light to work correctly. i used a lot of setuniforms, so there are probably some in there that were unnecesary, but i kept adding them in until it functioned properly. after the spotlight, i focused on the three point lights with different colors. i first tried simply making an array of different colors and then just updating and rendering the lighting each time, but i was unable to get that approach to work. my next approachh was to change how the uniforms worked inside of the shader itself, instead making an array of pointlight structs. this allowed me to create three separate objects, and loop through the point lights and update each uniform that needed to be changed in order to change the color of the lighting. then i had to figure out how to change the color of the cube. after some trial and error, i eventually found that i simply needed to change the light_fragment shader to include a uniform called lightColor so that i could manually tell the shader what color to make the light cube each time. finally, i checked that my directional light was stil. working properly by changing the values to absurd values so that a change would be noticeable. sine it was still working, i changed them back to their original values. i also added in some things to the camera controls, adding directional movement up and down by using the spacebar and left control respectively. i think this makes moving the camera around easier and more like how many modern games control when using a free cam.
